{
  "campaign": "common_dose_containment_v3",
  "platform": "classic_cruise_1900",
  "description": "Fit one common norovirus dose-response across all four hull classes on the onset-anchored model (PR #334: shedding curves read on their own days-since-onset axis, bounded pre-symptomatic windows, a real norovirus incubation kernel, and the wearable phase curve moved onto the same axis), on top of the hourly clock, the unit-safe reservoir/behaviour/cost parameters, per-partner direct-contact dose, and inhaled-air-volume airborne dose. Pathogen biology is identical in every cell: one profile, one dose ladder, applied unchanged to expedition/classic/spirit/mega. What differs operationally is quarantine compliance, swept as four named response branches on top of the same syndromic surveillance, plus a transmission-only counterfactual on the same cells so dose and containment stay separable. The ladder moves down from v2's 4.5-8.0 to 3.0-7.0: with a latent period restored, local probes put the expedition VSP crossing near dose 3.5-4.0 and the classic crossing near 5.0, so v2's grid would have been mostly extinctions at the small end. Seeds are held out from every diagnostic and from v1/v2.",
